fix-vendor-auth-entity-break: add the missing 'break' for VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

EntityGetAuthValue() falls through from the VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE
case into 'default' (FAIL(FATAL_ERROR_INTERNAL)), so an authorization with
the authValue of the vendor-specific TPM_RH_AUTH_xx handle (Part 2,
TPM_RH_AUTH_00..TPM_RH_AUTH_FF) puts the TPM into failure mode instead of
being checked.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
@@ -204,6 +204,11 @@ EntityGetAuthValue(TPMI_DH_ENTITY handle,  // IN: handle of entity
                 case VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE:
                     // vendor authorization value
                     pAuth = &g_platformUniqueAuth;
+                    // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT
+                    // determinism): upstream falls through into 'default' (which
+                    // enters failure mode), so the vendor authorization value is
+                    // never used.
+                    break;
 #endif
                 default:
                     // If any other permanent handle is present it is
